    <p>Under the <strong>Registration Act of 1908</strong> and <strong>Transfer of Property Act of 1882</strong>, verifying title deeds and encumbrances is the foundational step for any real estate transaction in India. An Encumbrance Certificate (EC) serves as an official legal transcript issued by the Sub-Registrar Office (SRO) within whose jurisdiction the property resides.</p>
    <ul style="padding-left: 20px; line-height: 1.8;">
